248807.missionDescription:
AYES, a multinational engineering and technology consultancy, is looking for Electromechanical Engineers and Consultants to join our growing team in Brussels, Belgium.
We operate globally across a wide range of industries, supporting our clients throughout the entire product and project lifecycle, from engineering and design to development, integration, testing and implementation.
We are looking for motivated Electromechanical Engineers with between 1 and 5 years of professional experience, who are eager to work on challenging engineering projects and develop their expertise in a dynamic, international environment.

The Role 
As an Electromechanical Engineer, you will work on multidisciplinary engineering projects where mechanical and electrical systems come together. Depending on your background and experience, you may contribute to the design, development, integration, testing and optimisation of electromechanical systems and components.You will work closely with engineers from different disciplines, contributing to technical solutions and supporting projects from the initial requirements through to implementation and validation. This is an opportunity for engineers who enjoy solving complex technical problems, working across engineering disciplines and turning technical requirements into practical solutions.

Key Responsibilities
Contribute to the design and development of electromechanical systems and components;
Analyse technical requirements and translate them into engineering solutions;
Support the integration of mechanical, electrical and electronic components;
Perform technical analyses and contribute to system-level problem solving;
Support testing, validation and troubleshooting activities;
Review technical specifications, drawings and engineering documentation;
Collaborate with Mechanical, Electrical, Electronics, Systems and other engineering teams;
Support the resolution of technical issues throughout the project lifecycle;
Contribute to technical reviews and project meetings;
Prepare and maintain technical documentation and engineering reports;
Support continuous improvement and optimisation of existing systems and solutions.

